        "title": "iPSCs: Yamanaka Factors and Reprogramming",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "In 2006, Shinya Yamanaka demonstrated that fully differentiated adult fibroblasts could be converted to pluripotent stem cells by introducing just four transcription factors. This was one of the most surprising discoveries in modern biology — it proved that developmental commitment is not irreversible."
    },
    {
      "id": "08-IPSCS.md#003",
      "path": [
        "08-IPSCS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:developmental-biology:08-ipscs, git-history:developmental-biology:08-ipscs]",
        "canonical_path": "developmental-biology/08-IPSCS.md",
        "concepts": "[ipscs]",
        "current_path": "developmental-biology/08-IPSCS.md",
        "id": "maxim:developmental-biology:ipscs",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "developmental-biology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[ipscs]",
        "section": "developmental-biology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "iPSCs: Yamanaka Factors and Reprogramming",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n+──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────+\n|              iPSC REPROGRAMMING OVERVIEW                         |\n|                                                                  |\n|  NORMAL DEVELOPMENT (one way)                                    |\n|  Zygote → ESC → Progenitors → Differentiated cells               |\n|                                                                  |\n|  YAMANAKA (reversed the arrow, 2006)                             |\n|  Fibroblast + Oct4 + Sox2 + Klf4 + cMyc → iPSC                   |\n|  Any somatic cell → pluripotent stem cell                        |\n|                                                                  |\n|  iPSC PROPERTIES                                                 |\n|  • Pluripotent (can make all cell types)                         |\n|  • Self-renewing                                                 |\n|  • Patient-specific (avoid immune rejection)                     |\n|  • Ethical alternative to ESCs (no embryo destruction)           |\n|                                                                  |\n|  iPSC → Neurons, cardiomyocytes, hepatocytes, beta cells, etc.   |\n|         Disease modeling, drug screening, cell therapy           |\n+──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────+\n```"
    },
